From e74f386c6320608746062cbbdd05175dbf16b275 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:24:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] linkbus: review fixes (validation, replay, stale run, SAB
 barrier)

Fixes from the independent review of d3c70df2e and aed3de564:

- Multiboard teardown: ~Multiboard no longer calls requestExit(); every
  backend destructor signals exit, so the native shm path stores exit and
  notifies once, as at 8412d3d8a. InMemoryBoard and SabBoard gain
  destructors that request exit.
- peekHubTick (mailbox and in-memory seat) trusts only frames that pass
  checkAssembledFrame for the seat (target, session, edition, geometry,
  size); otherwise it returns the last trusted tick.
- hubTick is documented as strictly monotonic for a sessionTag's life (a
  restarted hub must issue a new tag). A mailbox seat reports a link error
  after MailboxConfig::maxStaleRun (default 120) consecutive well-formed
  frames refused only as stale (Stats::staleTick).
- checkSlotFrame refuses slotSize * slotCount > kMaxPayload; the mailbox
  seat does not send such frames. InMemoryHub::submit takes the sender
  from the transport (fromNode) and refuses a mismatched nodeId and a
  localFrame that is not newer (replay, Stats::replayed).
- InMemoryHub clamps delayFrames to kMaxDelayFrames (600) and releases by
  tick distance, so stamps near wraparound do not release early.
- Mailbox take() treats seq 0 from the pull as no new frame.
- SAB barrier waits until the generation changes or time runs out, and a
  timed-out board withdraws its arrival bit (ok if the barrier completed
  meanwhile).
- InMemoryBoard::directData() returns nullptr so dmaStart uses the clamped
  copyOut().
- linkbus_install_mailbox and the SAB multiboard factory check that the
  buffers are SharedArrayBuffers of at least the layout sizes.

Tests: 12 new regression tests in tests/linkbus (several from the
reviewer's adversarial cases); run-tests.sh accepts LINKBUS_TEST_FLAGS for
sanitizer runs.

